@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "integration"

Feature: Liferay Support Sites integration
	Testing to assure that Liferay Support sites are integrated

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
    * I generate several random static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate static full start and end dates
	* I generate future static start and end dates
	* I generate future static full start and end dates
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticRandomScreamName} |
	| Email Address | ${staticRandomEmail}      |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstName} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastName}  |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "${staticRandomProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "${staticRandomProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                    |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "${staticRandomProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP OEM                           |
	| DXP Limited                       |
	| DXP Non-Production                |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ${staticProjectCode} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| ${staticAccountCode} |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| ${staticRandomEmail} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| ${staticRandomEmail} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| ${staticRandomEmail} |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| ${staticRandomEmail} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| ${staticRandomEmail} |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomAccountName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| ${staticRandomEmail} |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| ${staticAccountCode} |
	| ${staticProjectCode} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId4}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Assure Connection from Dossiera and Okta to Koroneiki
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the Connection from Dossiera and OKTA to Koroneiki is working properly

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | ${staticRandomAccountName}                 |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | ${staticRandomEmail}                       |
	| Contact First Name                     | ${staticContactFirstName}                  |
	| Contact Last Name                      | ${staticContactLastName}                   |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | ${staticRandomEmail}                       |
	| Owner First Name                       | ${staticContactFirstName}                  |
	| Owner Last Name                        | ${staticContactLastName}                   |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | ${staticRandomProjectName}                 |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.4                                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "${staticRandomProjectName}" and the following values
	| Account Field and Value    | liferayVersion             | DXP 7.4 | |
	| Code                       | ${staticProjectCode}       |         | |
	| Parent Account Name        | ${staticRandomAccountName} |         | |
	| Contact Email Address      | ${staticRandomEmail}       |         | |
	| Name                       | ${staticRandomProjectName} |         | |
	| Region                     | United States              |         | |
	| Language                   | English                    |         | |
	| Status                     | Active                     |         | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "${staticRandomEmail}" on the account "${staticRandomProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Support User |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	Then the support organization with the code "${staticProjectCode}" should be part of the support site
	And the user with the email address "${staticRandomEmail}" should be a member of the okta group "Customers"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "${staticRandomEmail}" and the following values
	| Email Address | ${staticRandomEmail}      |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstName} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastName}  |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "${staticRandomProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "${staticRandomProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |

Scenario: Assure Connection from Koroneiki to Provisioning
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the Connection from Dossiera and OKTA to Koroneiki is working properly

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | ${staticProjectCode}       | |
	| Name   | ${staticRandomProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States              | |
	| Status | Active                     | |
	| Tier   | T1                         | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "${staticRandomEmail}" on the account "${staticRandomProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support User |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "${staticRandomProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "${staticRandomProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "${staticRandomProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	Then I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "${staticRandomProjectName}"
	And I click on the account with the name "${staticRandomProjectName}" on the provisioning index

Scenario: Assure Connection from Koroneiki to Customer
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the Connection from Dossiera and OKTA to Koroneiki is working properly

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | ${staticProjectCode}       | |
	| Name   | ${staticRandomProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States              | |
	| Status | Active                     | |
	| Tier   | T1                         | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "${staticRandomEmail}" on the account "${staticRandomProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support User |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "${staticRandomProjectName}"
	| ${staticRandomEmail} |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "${staticRandomProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "${staticRandomProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "${staticRandomProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	Then the support organization with the code "${staticProjectCode}" should be part of the support site
	When I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a project with the name "${staticRandomProjectName}" and following values
	| Project Name          | ${staticRandomProjectName} |
	| Code                  | ${staticProjectCode}       |
	| Tier                  | T1                         |
	And the contact with the email address "${staticRandomEmail}" should be assigned the account "${staticRandomProjectName}"

Scenario: Assure Connection from Koroneiki to Zendesk
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the Connection from Dossiera and OKTA to Koroneiki is working properly

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | ${staticRandomAccountName}                 |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | ${staticRandomEmail}                       |
	| Contact First Name                     | ${staticContactFirstName}                  |
	| Contact Last Name                      | ${staticContactLastName}                   |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | ${staticRandomEmail}                       |
	| Owner First Name                       | ${staticContactFirstName}                  |
	| Owner Last Name                        | ${staticContactLastName}                   |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | ${staticRandomProjectName}                 |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.4                                        |
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync to be more reliable. Analyze if can be taken out once the account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should be synced to zendesk
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the subject "New Business: New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the text "Account Name: ${staticRandomProjectName}" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the text "Account Code: ${staticProjectCode}" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the text "Opportunity Type: New Business" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the text "New DXP Production (1)" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the text "New Platinum Subscription" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the text "Start Date - End Date: ${staticStartYear}" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the text "US Provisioning - Working with 2019 H2 Pricing Promotions: Grow Link" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the requester with the email address "provisioningrequest@liferay.com"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the organization "Provisioning"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the product "prd_provisioning_request"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the provisioning component "opportunity_invoiced"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the support region "provisioning_united_states"
	And the ticket with keywords "New Subscription(s) for ${staticRandomProjectName}" should have the primary address country "United States"
